Backport of r-wasm's webR fix for vroom: commit d0640b2 on the webr branch of
https://github.com/r-wasm/vroom ("Force deferred policy for std::async() in webR",
George Stagg; MIT), which rwasm builds for repo.r-wasm.org (its webr-remotes list).
CRAN's vroom starts its indexing and writing work with std::async(std::launch::async),
which needs a thread; webR's side modules have none, so every vroom() call -- and with
it readr::read_csv() -- fails with "thread constructor failed: Not supported". Under
Emscripten the patch launches that work deferred, on the calling thread.
`patch` ignores this text before the first diff header.

